{"nodes": [{"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_chapter7", "label": "Chapter 7 \u2014 The arithmetic encoding", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter7-arithmetic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_prime_encoding", "label": "N(x) = \u220f p\u1d62^{x\u1d62} \u2014 \u039b as a sublattice of a divisor lattice", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter7-arithmetic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not by analogy but exactly: order is divisibility, join is lcm, meet is gcd, rank is \u03a9."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_omega_and_small_omega", "label": "\u03a9 and \u03c9 appear as \u039b's rank and a bound on its dimension", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter7-arithmetic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Neither was placed there."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_occupancy_measure", "label": "d(x, y) = \u03c4(lcm/gcd) \u2014 the occupancy measure", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter7-arithmetic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It works exactly where an ordinary distance fails: the coordinate orders share only 0.3% of pairs, but every pair has a meet and a join, so the interval is total where the order is partial."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_d_x_x_equals_one", "label": "d(x, x) = 1, and it is not a convention", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter7-arithmetic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A point has no volume, but it is one point and it counts itself; the measure counts occupied cells."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_five_equivalent_forms", "label": "Five equivalent forms of d \u2014 interval, coordinate, two-integer, rational, p-adic", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter7-arithmetic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_log_d_metric", "label": "log d is an \u2113\u00b9 metric, and the balls are hyperbolic", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter7-arithmetic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_mobius_closed_form", "label": "The M\u00f6bius function in closed form off the seventeen-element poset", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter7-arithmetic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No recursion is needed for a 976-cell lattice; the answer comes from a seventeen-element poset."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_mobius_transfer_condition", "label": "Lattice and arithmetic M\u00f6bius agree iff the interval is a void-free unit hypercube", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter7-arithmetic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "60 void-free pairs agree, 56 void-bearing pairs disagree, no mixed case, decidable in seven comparisons."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_interval_carries_less", "label": "An interval carries less than the coordinates do, not more", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter7-arithmetic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Which is why it is a bound on where something already is, never a proposal of an unlisted cell."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_figure_7_1", "label": "Figure 7.1 \u2014 the occupancy measure", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter7-arithmetic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_chapter7", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_prime_encoding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter7-arithmetic.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_chapter7", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_omega_and_small_omega", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter7-arithmetic.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_chapter7", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_occupancy_measure", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter7-arithmetic.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter7_arithmetic_chapter7", "target": "drive_the_me